From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] engine: bare_app: the frame limit of the game's options

bare_app can hold a game to at most so many frames a second (the Options
tab of its controls screen, game_ipc.h frame_us). The platform waits for
it before each frame it publishes: game_shm_pace() of bare_app's
game_ipc.h. fps_max still counts as well; the lower of the two wins.

--- a/engine/platform/bare_app/bare_app.c
+++ b/engine/platform/bare_app/bare_app.c
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 	struct game_shm *shm;
 	size_t size;
 	unsigned back; // the frame the renderer draws into
+	struct game_pace pace; // bare_app's frame limit (game_shm_pace)
 	qboolean pad_down[GP_COUNT];
 	short axes[GP_AXIS_COUNT];
 	double repeat_time; // when a held D-pad direction repeats next, 0 - none
@@ -180,6 +181,9 @@
 
 	BareApp_DrawCursor( );
 
+	// bare_app's frame limit (the game's options): no sooner than that
+	// after the frame before
+	game_shm_pace( ba.shm, &ba.pace );
 	ba.back = atomic_exchange( &ba.shm->middle, ba.back | GAME_SHM_FRESH ) & ~GAME_SHM_FRESH;
 
 	// a full socket already holds a "frame" message, nothing to add
